else would I don't know if you want to go first before me. All right.

02:17:37.886 --> 02:17:41.163
I'm DJ, more commonly known as Duncan Searcy.

02:17:41.677 --> 02:17:44.891
I've missed you guys. It's been a little while since I've been to one

02:17:45.391 --> 02:17:48.120
of these, so I thought I'd come harass you. No, I'm going to be pretty

02:17:48.620 --> 02:17:52.314
nice. I want to talk a little bit about your proposed property tax increase,

02:17:52.988 --> 02:17:56.845
the reasons for doing it, and ask some questions, and then just inform

02:17:57.345 --> 02:18:01.215
you guys a little bit about what's going on in the life of the regular

02:18:01.424 --> 02:18:04.247
Eagan Eagle Mountaineer. Eagle Mountaineer, okay? So,

02:18:05.112 --> 02:18:08.896
220% is a lot. We will start there. Even if it's

02:18:09.396 --> 02:18:13.272
just $1 a day, for some of your citizens, that's 1 to 5% of

02:18:13.288 --> 02:18:16.142
their annual income, okay? So, that's,

02:18:16.575 --> 02:18:19.492
that's not a small chunk of change to some of us, some of us poor

02:18:19.992 --> 02:18:23.741
folk, okay? The other thing I want to mention is more

02:18:23.805 --> 02:18:27.748
of your neighbors than you realize are living paycheck to paycheck

02:18:27.796 --> 02:18:31.554
right now. Another good chunk, less hopefully,

02:18:31.971 --> 02:18:35.809
are living credit card payment to credit card payment. Every time

02:18:35.921 --> 02:18:39.132
you do anything to raise taxes, there's going to be

02:18:39.632 --> 02:18:43.195
effects, especially on our pensioners. They've earned what they

02:18:43.211 --> 02:18:46.775
have. If we're raising the property taxes on them, perhaps they

02:18:47.275 --> 02:18:50.099
moved here 15 years ago, and that was one of the calls to move out

02:18:50.131 --> 02:18:53.247
here to Eagle Mountain, is they saw the low property taxes. Okay,

02:18:53.504 --> 02:18:56.876
I do not think it is the job of the citizens to

02:18:57.376 --> 02:19:00.890
shoulder the burden of bad decisions past

02:19:01.390 --> 02:19:05.129
and present council city planning has made and

02:19:05.209 --> 02:19:09.047
force us to come up with those funds. We are growing rapidly.

02:19:09.625 --> 02:19:12.964
There should be a commensurate amount of tax

02:19:12.997 --> 02:19:16.674
increase there as well. Mayor Jarrett, when he was campaigning on

02:19:16.690 --> 02:19:20.425
the trail, he talked a lot about the different things that are coming, and we're

02:19:20.925 --> 02:19:23.153
going to have so much money we don't know what to do with. So maybe

02:19:23.653 --> 02:19:27.672
let's hold off on the property tax increase, wait for some of those investments

02:19:28.172 --> 02:19:31.772
to come, put the city hall on the back burner, some of these

02:19:32.272 --> 02:19:34.435
other things, while your citizens are really struggling financially.

02:19:35.973 --> 02:19:39.093
The other thing that I was going to say about all that

02:19:39.755 --> 02:19:43.490
is I think another reason the citizens are

02:19:43.990 --> 02:19:47.727
upset is the way it was framed. You guys are like, law enforcement, we love

02:19:48.227 --> 02:19:51.499
law enforcement, we need to increase that. But we had to find out

02:19:51.999 --> 02:19:55.511
in the comments that it was also for capital projects, and that wasn't defined anywhere,

02:19:56.137 --> 02:19:59.636
at least initially. And so it's kind of a bait and switch when you say

02:19:59.684 --> 02:20:03.038
we need to raise taxes so we have law enforcement, because who doesn't

02:20:03.538 --> 02:20:06.569
want a good amount of law enforcement? We want to be safe, right? So I

02:20:07.069 --> 02:20:09.940
felt like that was a little bit dishonest. 10 seconds remaining. And it rubbed people

02:20:10.440 --> 02:20:13.825
the wrong way there. So I think a little bit more

02:20:13.873 --> 02:20:18.113
transparency would do you well. I feel

02:20:18.145 --> 02:20:22.128
safe here. You know, I know they want more deputies. I genuinely

02:20:22.321 --> 02:20:25.710
don't feel threatened for my life. And if there's anybody here that

02:20:26.210 --> 02:20:30.271
has death threats, you know, that's me. So I think when we see

02:20:30.367 --> 02:20:33.402
so many patrol cars at a traffic stop,

02:20:33.884 --> 02:20:37.690
you know, 2, 3, 4, from the citizen's perspective,

02:20:37.755 --> 02:20:40.838
it doesn't look like we really need more law enforcement. Your time is

02:20:40.935 --> 02:20:44.425
up. Thank you. All right, thank you. Thank you.

02:20:45.396 --> 02:20:49.583
That's

02:20:50.083 --> 02:20:53.465
it. Was there anyone else here who did not have the opportunity to make public

02:20:53.965 --> 02:20:57.541
comment that would like to? Seeing no one, we will close

02:20:57.606 --> 02:21:01.495
the public comment period at 7:19 and

02:21:01.995 --> 02:21:06.205
bring it back to the council for comments to

02:21:06.705 --> 02:21:09.407
the public. And I'm going to switch sides. We're going to go with Rich first.

02:21:09.714 --> 02:21:13.672
Rich Wood. Great to see so many people

02:21:14.172 --> 02:21:15.851
here, especially those here to support the Youth Council.

02:21:17.477 --> 02:21:20.666
We appreciate their willingness to get involved at an early age to

02:21:20.682 --> 02:21:24.179
understand how government works. I love

02:21:24.276 --> 02:21:27.294
the way that we changed it to make it available for so many people to

02:21:27.794 --> 02:21:31.318
participate on the council. So it was great having

02:21:31.334 --> 02:21:34.524
them all up here. I'm a little envious, Jesse.

02:21:34.588 --> 02:21:36.985
I hope it's awesome this year for you guys.

02:21:37.179 --> 02:21:40.531
Appreciate the comments, DJ. Always appreciate

02:21:40.564 --> 02:21:43.354
you coming and speaking your mind. That's the point of public comments.

02:21:45.137 --> 02:21:47.894
I'm gonna tell you, I don't think that you're totally wrong. I think that we

02:21:47.958 --> 02:21:50.119
could have done a better job in some of the ways that it was presented.

02:21:51.150 --> 02:21:55.523
I look forward to being able to talk about that on Thursday and maybe

02:21:56.023 --> 02:21:59.175
providing some clarity, 'cause I agree. I think that it's not

02:21:59.224 --> 02:22:02.443
clear. So we're going to try to do a better job of getting that information

02:22:02.943 --> 02:22:06.925
so that it's clear. May not agree, but the reality of it is, is we

02:22:07.425 --> 02:22:08.413
need to be crystal clear.

02:22:12.098 --> 02:22:15.246
Councilmember Whiting. I'm so proud

02:22:15.746 --> 02:22:19.643
of the youth that are taking their time to be engaged and make

02:22:20.143 --> 02:22:22.834
a difference. And we saw that with our Youth Council. We see that with our—

02:22:23.600 --> 02:22:27.199
also with the pageants, and so awesome.

02:22:28.515 --> 02:22:32.160
There's a lot of energy with Youth Council, and it's really— I'm really honored to

02:22:32.690 --> 02:22:36.110
be the liaison from the City Council to be a part of your group,

02:22:36.126 --> 02:22:39.321
and looking forward to the activity that's going to happen tomorrow, even though I'm going

02:22:39.821 --> 02:22:43.207
to get wet and it's going to be cold. But really grateful.

02:22:43.287 --> 02:22:46.948
I mean, Eagle Mountain City has some of the most amazing

02:22:47.045 --> 02:22:50.887
youth, and I know it's a priority among the City Council to Create an

02:22:50.919 --> 02:22:54.557
environment here in which they can engage and learn, and there's

02:22:55.057 --> 02:22:58.663
a lot that's that we're dealing with to help keep them safe, help our

02:22:59.163 --> 02:23:02.641
roads improve. And so I won't go into the

02:23:03.141 --> 02:23:05.688
depth of all of what we need to continue to do to help this be

02:23:06.188 --> 02:23:07.768
the most amazing place ever for for the youth.

02:23:09.440 --> 02:23:12.366
Also, DJ, thanks for your comments, and we we appreciate you,

02:23:13.211 --> 02:23:16.556
you know, coming and sharing. And I will say,

02:23:17.871 --> 02:23:21.399
we could say in some ways, you know, what you

02:23:21.899 --> 02:23:25.569
mentioned about the money coming in eventually, that is true. And Mayor Gray did make

02:23:26.069 --> 02:23:28.664
comments that, you know, as data center money matures, it will come in.

02:23:29.369 --> 02:23:31.759
But I was also there many times when he said the next 4 years are

02:23:32.259 --> 02:23:34.790
probably going to be the most— the toughest years. And he also said, I'm probably

02:23:34.822 --> 02:23:37.837
going to be a one-term mayor, even if he wants a second term,

02:23:37.853 --> 02:23:41.446
because of the challenging decisions we're going to have to make during these current

02:23:41.946 --> 02:23:45.588
4 years because the data center money isn't here

02:23:45.700 --> 02:23:48.943
yet. And it's going to start maturing. It's going to start coming here.

02:23:49.007 --> 02:23:52.331
But we, you know, looking at the different things we got going on,

02:23:53.583 --> 02:23:57.131
we may have to make some unpopular decisions. And hopefully a

02:23:57.631 --> 02:24:00.294
lot of people show up on Thursday night. Hopefully we hear a lot of commentary

02:24:00.310 --> 02:24:02.895
from a lot of people because we want to hear what your thoughts are and

02:24:03.395 --> 02:24:06.829
what you're experiencing and what— yeah, your various

02:24:07.329 --> 02:24:09.563
thoughts and feelings. Please Please come on Thursday night. We want a big crowd,

02:24:09.628 --> 02:24:14.200
we want a lot of comments, and we're here to listen. So hopefully

02:24:14.458 --> 02:24:15.649
people show up and participate.

02:24:18.659 --> 02:24:21.737
Thanks, Mayor. Welcome, KJ. I just

02:24:22.237 --> 02:24:24.912
want to congratulate you, or should I say Mayor Call? Let me start there.

02:24:26.800 --> 02:24:29.795
That's quite an achievement. I'm really proud of you, and having had the opportunity to

02:24:30.295 --> 02:24:34.061
work with the Youth Council last year, I'm I'm impressed

02:24:34.109 --> 02:24:37.561
with the recruiting that you've been about. So thank

02:24:38.061 --> 02:24:41.222
you to you and your advisors, your mother, and those other young men

02:24:41.270 --> 02:24:44.915
and young women that have been participating there. It's fun to see the Youth Council

02:24:44.963 --> 02:24:48.110
grow, and I will be there tomorrow if I can find my hair, okay?

02:24:48.817 --> 02:24:51.353
I mean, I gotta find my wig so that I can come and you guys

02:24:51.386 --> 02:24:54.179
can dunk me again. But I don't know if I'm gonna last as long as

02:24:54.679 --> 02:24:57.632
last year. You guys beat me up bad, but I enjoyed it.

02:24:57.969 --> 02:25:01.144
I really did. You really are the future of Eagle Mountain.

02:25:01.337 --> 02:25:05.376
I love listening to the, to the, to Miss Eagle Mountain

02:25:05.649 --> 02:25:09.192
and Miss Teen Eagle Mountain as they talked about at least one of the CSIs.

02:25:09.416 --> 02:25:12.719
What do they call them? Community initiatives. Okay,

02:25:12.799 --> 02:25:15.893
about the wildlife and nature. And for me,

02:25:15.909 --> 02:25:19.468
that's really cool that our youth are picking up that torch and,

02:25:19.548 --> 02:25:22.979
and moving forward with it. So anything that I can do or anything that we

02:25:23.479 --> 02:25:26.798
can do as a council to help you all be successful and

02:25:26.894 --> 02:25:30.925
prepare you for adulthood, I'm happy to do that. I just want

02:25:31.425 --> 02:25:33.734
to express gratitude for our staff and for the work that they do, for the

02:25:34.234 --> 02:25:37.973
incredible burdens that they carry. If you joined us in work session, you got just

02:25:38.473 --> 02:25:41.666
a small taste of what they deal with on a daily basis,

02:25:41.682 --> 02:25:44.926
and it's a— it's an inexhaustible

02:25:45.135 --> 02:25:48.571
list of things that they have to tackle every day, and I'm really grateful for

02:25:48.587 --> 02:25:50.930
their energy and for their effort that they put forth.

02:25:51.860 --> 02:25:55.228
I'm grateful for the fellow council members that I sit here with. We are

02:25:55.728 --> 02:25:59.269
called upon to make some pretty, pretty nasty decisions. I don't know how else to

02:25:59.769 --> 02:26:03.407
say it. They're difficult, they're heavy, and I think it can

02:26:03.423 --> 02:26:06.230
best be described as there's a loneliness to leadership.

02:26:07.432 --> 02:26:10.046
When we ask for the opportunity to serve and to lead,

02:26:10.961 --> 02:26:13.895
it comes with a duty, a responsibility, a burden,

02:26:14.248 --> 02:26:17.474
and, and, and there's some honor and a blessing associated with it.

02:26:17.602 --> 02:26:20.958
But all of those things are present in the decisions that

02:26:20.990 --> 02:26:24.892
we make. And there's an accountability

02:26:25.069 --> 02:26:28.697
that each of us must have. And I think

02:26:29.197 --> 02:26:32.808
we can do better, DJ. Our communication could be better. I'm probably

02:26:32.856 --> 02:26:36.003
the worst communicator of all, unless you sit down with me across the

02:26:36.503 --> 02:26:39.616
table, and then I'll communicate you to death and you'll think I need a break.

02:26:40.178 --> 02:26:43.696
You'd be like, shut up, Brett, I'm ready to move on.

02:26:44.455 --> 02:26:47.754
But I just want to express my love and gratitude to those of you that

02:26:48.254 --> 02:26:51.003
have showed up today. I appreciate that, and I look forward to listening to what

02:26:51.503 --> 02:26:53.247
the citizens have to say on Thursday. Thank you.

02:26:55.991 --> 02:26:59.606
I too am super excited to see you be our youth mayor. I've seen

02:26:59.654 --> 02:27:03.744
you for years as I've come to Cedar Valley High School and seen

02:27:04.244 --> 02:27:08.541
you grow into student council and all sorts of

02:27:09.041 --> 02:27:11.809
other things, and I love that you and your colleagues are willing to serve our

02:27:11.874 --> 02:27:13.704
community and the other kids in our community.

02:27:14.860 --> 02:27:18.650
It's about time that Eagle Mountain has a youth council that's not embarrassingly

02:27:19.150 --> 02:27:22.808
small, and I'm super excited for that. And I'm really grateful

02:27:23.308 --> 02:27:26.630
for the young ladies that represent us as our city royalty.

02:27:27.144 --> 02:27:30.917
They're some pretty incredible young ladies, and they do really neat things in our community,

02:27:30.933 --> 02:27:34.530
so I'm grateful for them as well. This last Friday was

02:27:35.030 --> 02:27:38.913
our 28th wedding anniversary. My husband and I have been married for 28 years.

02:27:39.571 --> 02:27:42.734
And the day after that was my husband's birthday, and we got to go to

02:27:43.234 --> 02:27:46.957
see Spider-Man. That was like a big deal. And it's like

02:27:47.457 --> 02:27:50.586
the 12th Spider-Man. I don't even know. But as I

02:27:50.650 --> 02:27:54.247
was watching the movie, there's this line in Spider-Man

02:27:54.504 --> 02:27:57.683
that is kind of quintessential Spider-Man, and it says, with great power comes

02:27:58.183 --> 02:28:02.137
great responsibility. And I think one of the greatest powers that

02:28:02.218 --> 02:28:05.902
any human could be given is to tax another human being.

02:28:07.892 --> 02:28:11.514
It's your property. You worked hard to bring it home.

02:28:11.741 --> 02:28:16.124
You use it to take care of your family. And we don't take that

02:28:16.624 --> 02:28:17.420
responsibility lightly.

02:28:20.688 --> 02:28:22.057
Thank you.

02:28:24.364 --> 02:28:27.578
I want you to know that as we prepare to make

02:28:28.078 --> 02:28:31.419
this decision as a council, that we're thinking about you.

02:28:31.998 --> 02:28:35.883
We're thinking about your individual circumstances, and we're trying to do

02:28:36.109 --> 02:28:39.433
right by you and all of the residents of Eagle

02:28:39.933 --> 02:28:43.431
Mountain. And we take that

02:28:43.544 --> 02:28:47.072
responsibility really seriously. So thank you for being

02:28:47.104 --> 02:28:50.378
here today, and thank you for sharing your viewpoints. And I

02:28:50.878 --> 02:28:54.364
look forward to hearing all the ideas and insights

02:28:54.573 --> 02:28:57.981
and concerns on Thursday so that we can make this decision

02:28:58.029 --> 02:28:58.431
together.

02:28:58.980 --> 02:29:02.457
Thank you.

02:29:02.974 --> 02:29:04.769
Thanks everyone for being here today.

02:29:07.076 --> 02:29:10.566
To the Miss Eagle Mountain, they— it looks like they left. My daughter served as

02:29:11.066 --> 02:29:14.507
a Teen Eagle Mountain, Miss Eagle Mountain Teen.

02:29:15.881 --> 02:29:19.020
in 2019, and they— she served 2 years

02:29:19.052 --> 02:29:22.596
because of the pandemic. They didn't have another one, so she got to go

02:29:23.000 --> 02:29:26.144
2 years, and it just like was never-ending thing. But it was a real,

02:29:26.420 --> 02:29:27.895
a real blessing for her and our family.

02:29:29.650 --> 02:29:32.301
Mayor, Mayor Call, congratulations.

02:29:32.559 --> 02:29:35.851
That's awesome. Did you speak at our memorial service? Yes.

02:29:35.963 --> 02:29:39.233
That was an awesome speech that you gave. I just wanted to mention that to

02:29:39.733 --> 02:29:43.552
you again publicly. That was really impressive. And not

02:29:44.052 --> 02:29:47.437
a surprise that you're serving as our youth mayor. So congratulations. That's awesome.

02:29:47.485 --> 02:29:49.452
I know, I know our youth council will be led well.

02:29:51.113 --> 02:29:54.366
DJ, thank you for being here. I think the more

02:29:54.898 --> 02:29:58.400
heads we have, the more comments, the more ideas, the better decision that we're going

02:29:58.416 --> 02:30:01.553
to make. It is— I'm not having any

02:30:01.585 --> 02:30:04.998
fun. I spent most of my weekend going back through

02:30:05.871 --> 02:30:09.185
every budget session that we are already have sat through

02:30:10.216 --> 02:30:13.452
and copied every dollar that was presented,

02:30:15.674 --> 02:30:19.514
gave it a name, put it in a spreadsheet. I've been through it several

02:30:19.562 --> 02:30:23.650
times, and I just want you to know that I take this decision pretty seriously,

02:30:24.329 --> 02:30:28.031
and I know that my fellow council members do. It wasn't long ago

02:30:28.531 --> 02:30:31.425
that my wife and I, if I had a $10 expense, I would call her

02:30:31.925 --> 02:30:34.293
and say, hey, do we have that in our bank account? Can I go to

02:30:34.793 --> 02:30:38.400
lunch today, or are we packing lunches? And we have

02:30:38.929 --> 02:30:43.485
2 Title I schools in our city that are

02:30:43.598 --> 02:30:47.415
paycheck to paycheck. And for many people, they won't be asking

02:30:47.993 --> 02:30:51.618
for assistance. They'll probably just cut their savings or put

02:30:52.118 --> 02:30:56.030
it on the credit card. And so we have a serious, serious decision

02:30:56.530 --> 02:31:00.120
to make on Thursday, and I am confident that we'll strike the right balance,

02:31:00.201 --> 02:31:03.956
both for the residents, for the city, and for

02:31:03.972 --> 02:31:08.257
the need. We just sat through a presentation with Ben,

02:31:08.337 --> 02:31:11.948
our city administrator. We have over 100 projects going

02:31:11.996 --> 02:31:15.623
on in the city, and these aren't just light fixing a curb or,

02:31:16.634 --> 02:31:19.699
or, um, you know, putting tar in a road. These are like

02:31:19.763 --> 02:31:23.214
major infrastructure projects

02:31:23.714 --> 02:31:26.728
that are going on, and they're not, they're not inexpensive. We're the 9th fastest growing

02:31:26.776 --> 02:31:29.506
city in America, in the United States.

02:31:30.357 --> 02:31:32.861
And when you start to dig down and look at all of the projects that

02:31:33.361 --> 02:31:37.116
are happening with 2/3 or 1/3 of the staff

02:31:37.616 --> 02:31:41.307
of other cities of our same size, it's pretty impressive. It's a miracle

02:31:41.807 --> 02:31:44.968
in my mind that this city is even like operating. I just applaud

02:31:45.468 --> 02:31:49.191
our staff. They do an amazing job. And prior to January of this year,

02:31:50.187 --> 02:31:53.577
I was totally oblivious to all the things that were happening. And now that I'm

02:31:54.077 --> 02:31:58.247
immersed in it, it's pretty impressive. So I'm

02:31:58.747 --> 02:32:00.179
confident we'll find the right balance.

02:32:02.019 --> 02:32:05.185
And I appreciate the emails. I've had several that have come through.

02:32:05.266 --> 02:32:07.915
I'm reading through them, I'm documenting them,

02:32:08.867 --> 02:32:12.289
and we're gonna make the right decision, the best

02:32:12.789 --> 02:32:15.535
decision that we can. So thank you.

02:32:16.853 --> 02:32:21.304
Okay. I'll say that was 100 capital

02:32:21.433 --> 02:32:24.724
or construction projects. There's almost 400 total projects with

02:32:25.224 --> 02:32:27.855
initiatives and— Right, that's a lot, right? Heavy lift.

02:32:28.433 --> 02:32:31.693
So yeah, it's, it's, uh, I'll just add

02:32:31.773 --> 02:32:35.017
just briefly, the Youth Council came in a couple weeks

02:32:35.517 --> 02:32:38.581
ago and I don't know if you say challenged me to the

02:32:38.597 --> 02:32:41.953
hot wing challenge or something like that, right? It's just fun

02:32:41.985 --> 02:32:45.258
being in the position that I get to meet with the youth as well every

02:32:45.758 --> 02:32:48.560
now and again and some of the other organizations in the city and spend some

02:32:49.060 --> 02:32:51.510
time. And man, we've got some really fun youth. They ask some hard questions.

02:32:51.590 --> 02:32:54.171
Most of them I didn't know the answers to. I didn't even know who my

02:32:54.671 --> 02:32:58.515
superhero was or whatever it's called because I don't watch Marvel or

02:32:59.015 --> 02:33:03.196
something. But anyway, there were some hard questions. But what

02:33:03.244 --> 02:33:07.508
did I say wrong? Because I don't know. But probably a cowboy,

02:33:07.668 --> 02:33:10.907
Mayor. It's probably a cowboy of some sort. Ask me about bull riding. Yeah,

